From f933a55861690191025a63af3331672fcde4c1e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpaluri <mpaluri@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:15:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] db: extend QM descriptor store to support multiple SCS
 streams per client

Extend m_controller_qm_descriptors from a flat (bssid, client_mac) map
to a three-level map keyed by (bssid, client_mac, descriptor_key), where
descriptor_key is a packed uint16_t encoding (scsid << 8 | source_type).

This allows CLIENT and APPLICATION sources to each hold an independent
descriptor for the same SCS ID simultaneously, while still rejecting a
duplicate Add from the same source type for the same SCS ID.

set_controller_qm_descriptor gains source_type and descriptor_config_type
parameters (both defaulted) so callers can declare the origin and scope of
each descriptor without breaking existing call sites.  The northbound
SetQMDescriptors handler now passes APPLICATION as the source type and
deduplicates incoming entries by (client_mac, scsid) rather than client_mac
alone.

Signed-off-by: Manaswini Paluri <mpaluri@qti.qualcomm.com>

